      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T05:08:48Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app,ui): a stock copy carries its source's reduced-fidelity flag; a fidelity refusal silences the sim; the colours read the tightened tolerance\n\n- SetStock, UpdateModel's propagation, CreateSetup's clone and\n  DeleteSetup's undo carry the chord error on the FromModel stock\n  itself; the project saves and loads it on the stock row, and a stock\n  from an older file adopts its source's flag on load. Deleting or\n  renaming the source no longer stops the laws tightening.\n- model_fidelity::program_tol: the program sim and the eye judge at\n  the gate's refusal when an op is refused for its model's fidelity,\n  so the named refusal is never joined by a gouge line off the same\n  material.\n- FieldView carries the verdict tolerance its colours are gated at;\n  machined_classes and the GPU/CPU eyes read it instead of DEV_TOL.\n\nProjects saved before #911 are left open on the issue (a file-format\ndecision); see docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-flag-gaps.md.\n\nRefs #1056\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
